# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Generated by the test harnesses. web/tests/samples/ is deliberately NOT
# ignored: those files are committed as manual-test fixtures, are entirely
# synthetic, and are regenerated by the make_*_samples.mjs scripts.
web/tests/ref/
web/tests/_check.js

# Processed EDI output — may contain PHI, must never be committed.
# De-identified output is listed too: the run only rewrites the loops it
# recognises, so a file whose patient data sits somewhere unexpected comes out
# named "deidentified" while still carrying it.
*_processed_*.edi
*_lds_*.edi
*_deidentified_*.edi

# Working notes for in-flight work — plans, extracted specs, and source material
# read while designing a feature. Kept in the repo so they survive a session and
# sit next to the code they describe, but not committed: they are scratch. The
# rest of docs/ IS tracked, and anything in here worth keeping gets promoted out
# of notes/ into it.
#
# Source material also has to stay out for its own reasons: the X12 companion
# guides under docs/notes/*-sources/ are third-party PDFs read as reference.
docs/notes/
.notes/

# Editors — local IDE state, not project configuration. JetBrains writes .idea/
# into any project it opens, and the module and VCS mapping files inside name
# this machine's paths, so they are wrong for anyone else who clones.
.idea/

# OS
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
